WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.220 --> 00:00:16.004
The first few months went by quickly.

2
00:00:16.724 --> 00:00:20.525
Although Tommy was a slow learner, he did not give up easily.

3
00:00:21.526 --> 00:00:23.906
One day, he was having trouble with Gub-Gub.

4
00:00:23.926 --> 00:00:25.647
"Dr. Dolittle?"

5
00:00:26.087 --> 00:00:28.748
he called out, holding the pig under his arm.

6
00:00:29.568 --> 00:00:32.471
Dr. Dolittle had his head in the wiff-waff's tank.

7
00:00:33.632 --> 00:00:34.652
So all Dr.

8
00:00:34.692 --> 00:00:37.415
Dolittle heard was this: "Duroo Duroo-roo?"

9
00:00:38.856 --> 00:00:41.358
Dr. Dolittle pulled his head out of the tank.

10
00:00:41.678 --> 00:00:42.879
He did not look happy.

11
00:00:42.899 --> 00:00:46.582
"I can't do it," he sighed.

12
00:00:46.602 --> 00:00:50.885
"The wiff-waff isn't able to help me learn the shellfish language."

13
00:00:52.006 --> 00:00:53.167
"But you can't give up!"

14
00:00:53.647 --> 00:00:54.388
Tommy pleaded.

15
00:00:56.936 --> 00:00:59.218
The doctor removed his goggles and gloves.

16
00:00:59.238 --> 00:01:03.321
"Well, there is one more hope," he said.

17
00:01:03.341 --> 00:01:05.882
"But we will have to wait and see."

18
00:01:05.902 --> 00:01:09.585
"Doctor, I don't know what's wrong with Gub-Gub."

19
00:01:10.125 --> 00:01:12.207
Tommy handed him the wiggling pig.

20
00:01:12.927 --> 00:01:14.668
The doctor looked Gub-Gub over.

21
00:01:14.688 --> 00:01:18.731
"He looks fine to me," Dr.

22
00:01:18.771 --> 00:01:19.792
Dolittle remarked.

23
00:01:19.812 --> 00:01:23.875
"I asked for a piece of cake and look what he gave me!"

24
00:01:24.335 --> 00:01:25.256
Gub-Gub cried.

25
00:01:27.208 --> 00:01:28.209
"Yes, Gub-Gub.

26
00:01:28.449 --> 00:01:32.171
I told Tommy to give that to you," the doctor said in return.

27
00:01:32.191 --> 00:01:34.953
"No! I hate apples!"

28
00:01:35.334 --> 00:01:36.174
pouted the pig.

29
00:01:36.194 --> 00:01:38.356
"You're on a diet.

30
00:01:38.836 --> 00:01:41.478
From now on, only fruits and vegetables for you!"

31
00:01:41.998 --> 00:01:43.379
the doctor said sternly.

32
00:01:44.359 --> 00:01:46.961
Just then, Polynesia flew into the room.

33
00:01:47.542 --> 00:01:48.482
She was breathless.

34
00:01:48.502 --> 00:01:51.124
"Oh, doctor!

35
00:01:51.584 --> 00:01:53.986
The purple she gasped.

36
00:01:54.006 --> 00:01:56.988
"Tell me, what is it, Polynesia?"

37
00:01:57.436 --> 00:01:58.377
the doctor urged.

38
00:01:59.438 --> 00:02:01.680
Polynesia took a few deep breaths.

39
00:02:03.641 --> 00:02:05.923
"The purple bird of paradise is here.

40
00:02:06.423 --> 00:02:08.225
She brings bad news!"

41
00:02:09.486 --> 00:02:11.127
"Oh, dear, oh, dear!"

42
00:02:11.627 --> 00:02:12.728
the doctor frowned.

43
00:02:13.309 --> 00:02:15.851
He dropped Gub-Gub and rushed into the kitchen.

44
00:02:16.631 --> 00:02:17.812
Tommy ran after.

45
00:02:19.253 --> 00:02:22.216
A beautiful purple bird was sitting on the table.

46
00:02:22.964 --> 00:02:28.287
Her head was decorated with a crown of gold that matched her long sweeping tail.

47
00:02:28.307 --> 00:02:30.849
"Miranda!" the doctor shouted.

48
00:02:33.230 --> 00:02:35.932
The beautiful bird dramatically opened one eye.

49
00:02:35.952 --> 00:02:38.133
"Dr. Dolittle!"

50
00:02:38.753 --> 00:02:39.334
she moaned.

51
00:02:40.374 --> 00:02:42.355
"Long Arrow has disappeared!"

52
00:02:43.616 --> 00:02:47.378
Dr. Dolittle swayed on his feet and fell into a chair.

53
00:02:47.398 --> 00:02:50.200
"Disappeared? What do you mean?"

54
00:02:50.956 --> 00:02:53.799
Tommy could see that the doctor was very upset.

55
00:02:53.819 --> 00:03:01.845
"Long Arrow doesn't go anywhere without telling us birds," Miranda continued.

56
00:03:01.865 --> 00:03:04.087
"But now he's gone!

57
00:03:04.928 --> 00:03:06.850
Not even a word to the eagles."

58
00:03:06.870 --> 00:03:10.253
"That doesn't make sense!"

59
00:03:10.733 --> 00:03:12.154
The doctor shook his head.

60
00:03:12.174 --> 00:03:16.057
"Long Arrow and the eagles are the closest friends!

61
00:03:16.618 --> 00:03:18.720
He always tells them where he is going."

62
00:03:20.144 --> 00:03:23.925
"That is why we fear the worst," the beautiful bird cried.

63
00:03:25.566 --> 00:03:27.866
Dr. Dolittle paced back and forth.

64
00:03:27.886 --> 00:03:33.428
"No. There has got to be some explanation," he kept muttering.

65
00:03:33.448 --> 00:03:36.048
"Where was the last place you saw him?"

66
00:03:36.068 --> 00:03:39.509
"On Spider Monkey Island," replied Miranda.

67
00:03:39.529 --> 00:03:41.710
"Then that is where he must be!"

68
00:03:42.310 --> 00:03:43.410
exclaimed the doctor.

69
00:03:43.430 --> 00:03:49.292
"We searched everywhere for the great Indian," said Miranda.

70
00:03:50.048 --> 00:03:52.209
"We flew over the entire island."

71
00:03:52.229 --> 00:03:57.430
"I believe no, I KNOW he is still there!"

72
00:03:57.950 --> 00:03:59.511
the doctor said stubbornly.

73
00:03:59.531 --> 00:04:03.652
"We will go to Spider Monkey Island and find Long Arrow!"

74
00:04:04.452 --> 00:04:07.153
At this point, Tommy could take it no longer.

75
00:04:07.173 --> 00:04:10.274
"Excuse me, Dr.

76
00:04:10.314 --> 00:04:12.194
Dolittle," interrupted Tommy.

77
00:04:12.214 --> 00:04:14.635
"Please tell me what's going on."

78
00:04:15.555 --> 00:04:17.976
The doctor turned to him and grabbed his shoulders.

79
00:04:18.592 --> 00:04:22.456
"Tommy, Long Arrow is missing and we are going to find him!"

80
00:04:22.476 --> 00:04:24.157
"Who is Long Arrow?"

81
00:04:24.638 --> 00:04:25.418
Tommy asked.

82
00:04:27.840 --> 00:04:31.924
"Long Arrow is the greatest naturalist in the world," said the doctor.

83
00:04:31.944 --> 00:04:33.826
"What's a naturalist?"

84
00:04:34.226 --> 00:04:34.827
asked Tommy.

85
00:04:34.847 --> 00:04:41.352
"A person who studies nature—plants, animals, insects, everything that lives."

86
00:04:41.973 --> 00:04:45.096
Tommy said, "Can he speak to animals like you?"

87
00:04:46.476 --> 00:04:48.977
"He can communicate with all forms of life.

88
00:04:49.877 --> 00:04:55.058
Long Arrow and I have communicated through Miranda for many years," continued the doctor.

89
00:04:55.078 --> 00:04:58.499
"I recently sent a message asking for his help."

90
00:04:58.519 --> 00:04:59.600
"For what?"

91
00:04:59.620 --> 00:05:03.361
"To understand the language of the shellfish.

92
00:05:03.901 --> 00:05:06.321
But now the great Long Arrow is missing.

93
00:05:06.801 --> 00:05:08.322
And," added Dr.

94
00:05:08.362 --> 00:05:13.423
Dolittle firmly, "it looks as if I will have to go and find my friend!"

95
00:05:13.443 --> 00:05:16.124
"Can I come with you?"

96
00:05:16.724 --> 00:05:18.186
Tommy asked excitedly.

97
00:05:19.128 --> 00:05:22.433
He had long dreamed of going off on a voyage with the doctor.

98
00:05:22.453 --> 00:05:26.218
"Yes, but we don't have much time," said Dr.

99
00:05:26.258 --> 00:05:29.543
Dolittle. Tommy could hardly believe it.

100
00:05:30.144 --> 00:05:32.667
He was finally going to travel the world.
